    "description": "Pembina Gas Infrastructure is a Western Canadian gas processing and midstream platform providing natural gas and natural gas liquids processing, transportation, and related services. Its customers are upstream producers in the Montney and Duvernay regions that need processing and takeaway capacity for natural gas and liquids production. The operating model is asset-heavy and fee-based, supported by large processing and transportation infrastructure with long-life industrial use and recurring customer throughput. Public company materials describe combined processing capacity of 5 billion cubic feet per day and a footprint extending from central Alberta to northeast British Columbia. Pembina and KKR formed the joint venture in 2022, with Pembina retaining 60% ownership and operating control and KKR's global infrastructure funds holding the remaining 40%.",
